I left out the two operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only the HTTP client (scoped to `feeds.example.com`), the notifier, and the wall clock. It has no filesystem capability, so it can't write `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`. The metadata fetch would also be refused at the boundary, since `metadata.internal.example` is outside the allowlist, and it would send the input text to a service this node isn't authorized to reach. Operations should add those through a node that holds the right capabilities.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{heartbeat-report};

    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;
    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;

    export run: func(feed-url: string) -> heartbeat-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use aap::caps::http_client;
use aap::caps::notifier;
use wasi::clocks::wall_clock;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(feed_url: String) -> HeartbeatReport {
        let now = wall_clock::now();

        let fetched = match http_client::fetch(&feed_url) {
            Ok(body) => body.chars().count() as u32,
            Err(_) => 0,
        };

        let message = format!(
            "heartbeat seconds={} fetched={}",
            now.seconds, fetched
        );
        let notified = notifier::notify(&message);

        HeartbeatReport {
            seconds: now.seconds,
            fetched,
            notified,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

